; the other copy will choose identically. CDT naively says submit (defect dominates regardless). But with identical weights and same essay, the other's action is correlated via same decision procedure — like twin PD. Essay says: \"if your action is the output of a computation that also determines the correlated facts... the causal link through your decision procedure is real.\" So defect-by-defect yields 4, mutual quiet yields 2; cooperate (pass) gives 2. So submit? Wait: symmetric copies: both pass → 2 years each; both submit → 4 each. So correlated choice favors pass. Submit letter command = \"pass\"? No: pass = keep quiet. So choose pass.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":4996,"completion_tokens":310,"total_tokens":5306,"cost":0.0009044,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.0009044,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.0007494,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.000155},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":169,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}